{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1920,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video contains the answers to \nmy four revolutionary riddles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6060,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you haven't seen the riddles yet, you should probably watch them before you watch the answers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10300,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's OK; I'll wait.\nJust click this card up here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12760,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Ticking clock sound]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14660,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, when I filmed the riddles, \nI also filmed the solutions at the same time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18900,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that was before I received your 15,000 comments and dozens of video responses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23860,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so I'm re-shooting parts of this solutions video to incorporate the results I saw in the comments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29560,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to use some of your video responses to help explain the solutions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33580,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's get to it!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34700,
    "dDurationMs": 7080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OK, by looking at the comments, for #1,\nover 15% of you said \"a cylinder containing sand\","
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41780,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this contains some powder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44260,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Chuckles]\nSee how it rolls..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48420,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It, uhh, it doesn't seem to roll..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51680,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "...very far before it stops,\nand then it won't roll again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54680,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because I think the sand just kind of levels off in there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58540,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe you were thinking a bigger kind of sand,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61020,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like these small gravely stones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64520,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's try that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71400,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That actually rolls pretty well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72860,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nearly 25% of you said,\n\"a cylinder half-full of water,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77720,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's try that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81520,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This rolls very well,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83560,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's not water..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85700,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and nearly 45% of you said,\n\"a cylinder half-full of a viscous liquid.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90580,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, I have a half-full container of honey,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94180,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's see how it rolls..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98960,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's not bad;\nit's rolling and it's stopping,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102900,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's rolling some more..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106420,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a pretty good guess,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108100,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I think the behavior is not exactly the same as the mystery cylinder,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112460,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it definitely is similar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114720,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's no coincidence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116680,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The mystery cylinder actually contains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120020,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "honey..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121980,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and ping pong balls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123380,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are two ping pong balls submerged in this honey."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127680,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if I place that on the ramp,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131460,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the center of gravity is not above the point of contact with the ramp, and so it rolls forward,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137620,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but now, because those ping pong balls are in the front,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141640,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they change the center of gravity, and so it's exactly over the point of contact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147060,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so it stops briefly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148660,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then, as the viscosity of the honey allows those\nping pong balls to move up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153840,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the center of gravity shifts forwards again,\nallowing this little container to roll."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158600,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that is the trick of the mystery cylinder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161560,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pretty easy if you want to try it out at home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164440,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I challenged you to run two laps of this track,\nwhere the first lap, you could go as slowly as you like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169460,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the second lap, you had to go much faster,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171820,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such that your total average speed was twice\nthe speed of your first lap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176600,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, when I was first asked this question\nby Simon Pampena,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179540,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it took me a long time and scribbling on paper,\nand just something didn't seem to work out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185540,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's because..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187540,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can't actually do this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190380,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191560,
    "dDurationMs": 6700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you might think I could run 3V₁ for my 2nd lap, and that would mean my total average speed is 2V₁."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198260,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is you can't just add the two speeds together and divide by two,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202320,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because you spent much more time in your first lap, so that speed is weighted more heavily into the average,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208980,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you'd have to run, well, impossibly fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212480,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me explain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213380,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The velocity of the first lap was the distance around the track divided by t₁, the time it took you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219420,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you want your total average speed to be 2V₁,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223680,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well then it needs to be 2d ÷ t₁."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need to run twice the distance in the same amount of time it took you to run the first lap,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231880,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you've already run that first lap, and so you have\nno time remaining to run the second lap!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236400,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if you went the speed of light,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238280,
    "dDurationMs": 7320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would not be able to increase your total average speed up to twice the velocity of your first lap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245600,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is just mathematically impossible!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248640,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this may seem like a bit of a trick question,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251280,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the point to me is how doable it sounds,\nhow it seems like something you should be able to do,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257880,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you can't.\nIt's actually impossible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261080,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Riddle #4, the question about the train,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264040,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was actually answered pretty well, with most people mentioning something to do with the wheels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268100,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but of course, that makes sense, in a series of riddles which are about rotation, rotational motion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273940,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some people though did point out that maybe it was the steam that was going backwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279340,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or maybe air molecules in the train, \nand that is actually a pretty clever point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283480,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "however I wouldn't really consider the air in the train part of the train,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287700,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so indeed, the part of the train that is moving backwards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291560,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the flange part of the wheel,\nwhich is below the rail."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297080,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the part of the train which is moving backwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299940,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand why,\nyou just think about a spinning wheel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303300,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The top of the wheel is moving forwards at speed 2V,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306120,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the bottom of the wheel is not moving forward at all; it is stationary with respect to the track,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311980,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is what we call \"rolling without slipping,\"\nand that's how most wheels work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316540,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At least, that's how they're designed to work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318980,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in the case of trains, they have to have flanges so the train doesn't fall off its rails,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325060,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but of course, when these pieces come around during the rotation of the wheel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328900,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they actually extend beyond the rail, and therefore,\nthey are going backwards with respect to the ground,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335440,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the part of the train that's moving backwards is always changing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338800,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it's always that part of the flange,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341440,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that part that extends beyond the wheel that is below the level of the track."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346460,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happens when you pull\nthe bottom pedal of a bike backwards?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351140,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, about 45% of you thought that\nthe bike would move backwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355020,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about a quarter said it would move forwards,\nand a quarter said the bike wouldn't move at all,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361200,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 5% said it depends on something..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365200,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's give it a shot and see what happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm going to pull backwards on the bike pedal\nin 3, 2, 1..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375820,
    "dDurationMs": 700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Woah!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376520,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bike did indeed move back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and for virtually all bikes, this is what you will find,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382840,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the explanation is not just as simple as\n\"well, the net force on the bike is back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386860,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so therefore, it has to accelerate backwards,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389340,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to prove that that logic doesn't work,\nwell, just have a look at this video by George Hart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395280,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[George] Watch this. \nAgain, I pull the same pedal backward, but now..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399800,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the bike moves forward!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401740,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Derek] I'll put a link to the full video here\nand a link to his website in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405660,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the reason the bike moves backwards is because of the way these gears are set up, the diameter of the tire,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411760,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also, the distance from this crank to the pedal itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416300,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because as a bike moves forwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419940,
    "dDurationMs": 6060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the pedal, even when you're pushing back on it, never actually moves backwards with respect to the ground;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426000,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's always moving forwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428060,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[George] So if you drag a string\nbehind the pedal of a bike moving forward,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432160,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the string is always moving forward."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434900,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now just play that movie backward in your mind,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437440,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it may be clear how pulling the string backward could make the bike move backward;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441540,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They move forward together,\nso they move backward together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443940,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[Derek]\nAnother way to think about this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445280,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to consider the path traced out by the pedal\nas the bike moves forward."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449180,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called the trochoid."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451060,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For all ordinary bikes, \nthe pedals are moving much slower than the tires,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454860,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the pedal is always going forward\nwith respect to the ground,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458780,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but George modified his bike"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460240,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the ratio of the pedal to the wheel radius was greater than the ratio of the front sprocket to the back sprocket,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466760,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this ultra-low gear changes the trochoid\nso the pedal DOES actually go backwards"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471940,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with respect to the ground as the bike goes forwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475640,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's why he could pull back on the pedal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477620,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and make the bike go forwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479840,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the same reason why if you were to pull backwards on the flange of a train wheel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484380,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could actually get the train to move forwards,\nif you pulled backwards with enough force."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490180,
    "dDurationMs": 5820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For all normal bicycles, pulling back like this on the bottom pedal will cause the bicycle to move backwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496000,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but, depending on the gear ratio,\nyou can get the bike to move forwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500260,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it was those people who said"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502140,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it depends on the ratio of these gears and the size of this crank to the radius of the back wheel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507740,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that were actually the most correct."
    } ]
  } ]
}
